    "detailedExplanation": "\n<h3>1. Section 54: 'Sale' Defined</h3>\n<p>'Sale is a transfer of ownership in exchange for a price paid or promised or part-paid and part-promised.'</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Parties:</strong> Buyer and Seller competent to contract.</li>\n  <li><strong>Subject-Matter:</strong> Tangible immovable property or reversion/intangible thing.</li>\n  <li><strong>Price (Money Consideration):</strong> The consideration must be money (price). If consideration is property in exchange for property, it is an <em>Exchange</em> (Section 118). If without consideration, it is a <em>Gift</em> (Section 122).</li>\n  <li><strong>Transfer of Ownership:</strong> All rights of ownership pass from seller to buyer.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>2. Mode of Transfer under Section 54</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Tangible Immovable Property of Value Rs. 100 or Upwards:</strong> Can be made <strong>only by a registered instrument</strong>. (Oral sale is void).</li>\n  <li><strong>Tangible Immovable Property of Value Less Than Rs. 100:</strong> Can be made either by a registered instrument or by <strong>delivery of the property</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Reversion or Other Intangible Thing:</strong> Can be made only by a registered instrument, regardless of value.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>3. Sale vs. Contract for Sale (Section 54, Para 3)</h3>\n<p>'A contract for the sale of immovable property is a contract that a sale of such property shall take place on terms settled between the parties.'</p>\n<p><strong>Crucial Indian Rule (Section 54, Para 4):</strong> <em>'It does not, of itself, create any interest in or charge on such property.'</em></p>\n<p>In English law, an agreement to sell creates an equitable estate in the purchaser. In India, there is no distinction between legal and equitable estates. A contract for sale creates <strong>only a personal right in personam</strong> to demand a registered conveyance; it conveys zero proprietary interest in the land (<em>Rambhau Namdeo Gajre v. Narayan Bapuji Dhotra, 2004 SC</em>).</p>\n",
