    "detailedExplanation": "\n<h3>1. Seller's Duties Before and After Completion (Section 55(1) & (2))</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Disclosure of Latent Material Defects (Section 55(1)(a)):</strong> Seller is bound to disclose to the buyer any <strong>latent material defect</strong> in the property or in the seller's title which the seller knows, and which the buyer could not with ordinary care discover. Failure to disclose is fraudulent!</li>\n  <li><strong>Production of Title Deeds (Section 55(1)(b)):</strong> Bound to produce all documents of title for examination on buyer's request.</li>\n  <li><strong>Answering Questions as to Title (Section 55(1)(c)):</strong> Bound to answer to the best of his information all relevant questions put by buyer regarding title.</li>\n  <li><strong>Care of Property (Section 55(1)(e)):</strong> Between contract and delivery of possession, bound to take as much care of the property as an ordinary prudent owner.</li>\n  <li><strong>Payment of Outgoings (Section 55(1)(g)):</strong> Bound to pay all public charges, taxes, and rents accrued up to the date of sale.</li>\n  <li><strong>Implied Covenant for Title (Section 55(2)):</strong> Seller is deemed to contract that the interest which he professes to transfer subsists and that he has power to transfer the same (runs with the land).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>2. Seller's Lien for Unpaid Purchase Money: Section 55(4)(b)</h3>\n<p>Where ownership has passed to the buyer before payment of the whole purchase money, the seller is entitled to a <strong>charge upon the property</strong> in the hands of the buyer, any transferee without consideration, or any transferee with notice, for the unpaid amount of the purchase money and interest.</p>\n\n<h3>3. Buyer's Charge for Prepaid Purchase Money: Section 55(6)(b)</h3>\n<p>The buyer is entitled to a <strong>charge on the property</strong>, as against the seller and all persons claiming under him, for the amount of any purchase money properly paid by the buyer in anticipation of delivery and for interest on such amount, unless he has improperly declined to accept delivery.</p>\n",
